# Every image copies build output that already exists on the host, so the
# context only needs sources, manifests and that output. node_modules is the
# expensive exception: pnpm's tree is symlinks into a store that means nothing
# inside an image, and each image installs its own.
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/.tmp
.git
.github

# The one node_modules that must ship. `output: "standalone"` writes a real
# dependency tree under here — not workspace symlinks into a store — and it is
# the only copy of Next the image gets. Excluding it builds an image that starts
# and then dies on "Cannot find module 'next'".
!apps/profile/.next/standalone/**

# The profile image needs apps/profile/.next/standalone, so .next stays. Its
# cache directory does not.
**/.next/cache
